+THE STRUCTURAL REFACTOR, AND WHAT IT DID TO THIS LEDGER
+-------------------------------------------------------
+The gated catalog rides the `Preview` record, snapshotted by `repropose`
+alongside `clockText`, because every consumer was downstream of a live
+preview. An earlier revision carried an entry for "the body memo tracks the
+tier (not just the catalog)"; that memo no longer exists, so the entry is
+gone because the hazard is gone — not because it stopped being checked. Two
+entries replace it: "the preview CARRIES the gated world it was solved
+against" (four rows) and "the pickers read the SOLVED snapshot, not the live
+tier" (one row).
+
+The refactor's headline guarantee is now pinned rather than merely asserted:
+a tier change that cannot re-propose — `repropose` returns early on an
+unparseable Rate — leaves the pickers and constrained rows describing the
+world the proposal was solved in. The TIER `<select>` is the deliberate
+exception: it binds the live tier, so it leads the solved world until the
+next successful propose. Both halves are asserted in the same row.
 
